            <div class="pdp-name">Nodulizer / Disc Pelletiser</div>
            <div class="pdp-tag">VECTOMEC™ Processing Range</div>
            <div class="pdp-desc">The nodulizer — also called a disc pelletiser or pan pelletiser — is an inclined rotating pan onto which fine powder is fed along with a controlled addition of water or binder. As the pan rotates, particles aggregate into small spherical balls (nodules or pellets) that grow to a target size, then discharge over the pan rim by centrifugal action. In VSK cement production, nodulising is an essential step: raw meal must be formed into uniform nodules of 8–20mm and mixed with coal before charging to the shaft kiln. Without consistent, strong nodules the kiln will not operate correctly. Jayveecons has been building nodulizers for VSK plants since 1987 and understands the exacting requirements of the nodulising step better than almost any other fabricator in India.</div>
