            <button class="pdp-close" onclick="toggleDetail('detail-airlock')"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg> Close</button>
            <div class="pdp-name">Rotary Air Lock</div>
            <div class="pdp-tag">VECTOMEC™ Support Range</div>
            <div class="pdp-desc">A rotary airlock (also called a rotary valve or star feeder) uses a slowly rotating multi-vane rotor inside a close-tolerance housing to transfer bulk material from one pressure zone to another while minimising air leakage between them. The rotor pockets fill with material at the inlet, rotate through approximately 180°, and discharge the material at the outlet — all while the rotor tips maintain a close running clearance with the housing that limits air bypass. They are indispensable wherever a pneumatic conveying system, dust collector, or pressurised process must accept or discharge material without losing its pressure seal. Jayveecons fabricates standard and drop-through rotary airlock configurations, with cast iron, fabricated steel, or stainless steel housings to match the material and duty.</div>
            <div class="pdp-specs-title">Typical Specifications</div>
            <div class="pdp-specs">
