            <div class="pdp-desc">Every driven piece of equipment in a bulk handling plant — conveyors, elevators, mixers, mills, kilns, and feeders — runs at a specific shaft speed that is almost always much lower than the speed of the electric motor driving it. The gearbox bridges this gap, reducing motor speed to the required output shaft speed while multiplying torque in proportion. Selecting the right gearbox involves matching the rated output torque and service factor to the application's actual load characteristics, and choosing the right mounting configuration (foot, flange, shaft-mount) for the installation. Jayveecons supplies helical, bevel-helical, and worm-and-wheel gear reducers sourced from quality manufacturers, and can pair them with the electric motor and coupling as a complete matched drive package for any of our conveying or processing equipment.</div>
