            <div class="pdp-desc">The screw flight is the helical blade that does the actual conveying work inside a screw conveyor — and in abrasive applications it is the primary wear item. As the flight wears, the clearance between flight OD and trough increases, material slips backward rather than being positively conveyed, and throughput falls. Eventually the flight wears through entirely. Jayveecons fabricates replacement screw flights to match your existing conveyor's pitch, diameter, shaft size, and hand (left or right). For high-wear duties — fly ash, cement raw meal, sand, clinker grit — we offer hard-faced flights (tungsten carbide or chromium carbide overlay on the leading face) and full AR steel (Hardox 400/450) flighting that lasts significantly longer than standard mild steel in abrasive service.</div>
